The title has a couple of meanings behind it;

1

I was transferred from Tsuyama, to Gobo. The most infamously Inaka
(country) part of the mission. Don't get me wrong, there could be a couple
places in our mission that have slightly less, but Gobo is the first place
people say when they think of small and far away areas. It's pretty dang
barren =F0=9F=98=82 Ever since I've heard about Gobo (and since I visited a=
 few times
for exchanges) I've always wanted to go =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82

2

This entire past week we were sick and had to stay in our apartment =F0=9F=
=92=80

Here's a few highlights since coming to Gobo =F0=9F=94=A5

On Christmas, we randomly greeted a young guy and ended up spending the
next like 6-8 hours with him, shared about the gospel and even ate out with
the Missionary Work Coordination leader and his wife with this guy =F0=9F=
=98=82 His
name is Jian! He came to church with us too, and it was awesome. He's a
really cool guy, 22 years old, likes to hang out, talk, and smoke. He
smokes 1 pack a month which isn't like crazy for a smoker by any means, but
he doesn't wanna stop to join our church. We haven't been able to
communicate wuth him for these past two weeks cause we don't have his
contact info (his phone is in need of repairs =F0=9F=98=82) but he knows ho=
w to reach
us. Hopefully we can just bump into him again soon, because it stinks that
it's hard to meet up consistently.

Elder Warnick (my new companion) is a fun guy =F0=9F=98=82 He is a bit of a=
 clean
freak and he hates his hair like 90 percent of the day, but he's really
focused in on missionary work. Seems like he hasn't had a chance to do much
of the approaching or speaking in missionary work yet, so I'm trying to
provide ample opportunity for him!

The members in Gobo are awesome!!! On new years we watched the sunrise of
the new year with the Kinoshita family, and then got to spend the whole day
eating a bunch of traditional food and playing games with them and their
family at their house all day! It was so fun, and made me feel pretty at
home for the first time in a while.

We have tried a few fun ways to meet with people! Spikeball missionary
work, drawing art for people, housing, bike streeting, a lot of good stuff!
This week even though we've been sick, a girl messaged us on a social media
app and wants to meet with us, so hopefully she can respond and we can meet
up!

Poetry Time

Wings are stick-on for some;
Fly for as long as you want, and then it's a
Peel-off the bandage type thing when you're done.

I wonder why wings bring shame to people.
Are the colors too bright? Do they not fold up just right?

Flight isn't a thing to be embarrassed about!
Its graceful and freeing, is it not?
Why can't you be happy with the great good that you've got??

Take pride in your wings and fly far far away
To a land filled with wings and where all of us say
"Our wings stick around."

I'm writing some of this on a train to Wakayama, and it's worth noting that
travel in Gobo is much easier and faster than Tsuyama =F0=9F=98=82 Tsuyama =
was like 4
hours to the nearest area and Gobo is like one. So it's definitely an
upgrade.

It's been a wild past few weeks, and honestly it doesn't feel like it's
been half of the transfer already =F0=9F=98=85 I'm sincerely hoping that we=
 will be
able to make a lot of solid time for finding and teaching in Gobo this next
few weeks. I'm really excited to share about it!

I know that God loves us and is desperate for us to turn to him. Even as a
missionary I feel like I need to make more room for Him in my day to day
life. I'd encourage you to as much as you can, seek to use your time in a
way that's spiritually enlightening. On Sunday we had a Zone devotional and
I was able to reflect on the experiences I've had dispelling darkness with
positive spiritual things. Darkness doesn't have to look dark, or even be
an inherently bad thing. But if it's not working towards bettering you as a
person, and it doesn't follow God's standards, it will work as a darkness
in your life if you are unconscious of it.

Be careful and evaluate what you're doing with your time, and pray about it
too. God will consecrate your efforts to be positive works of light.

I love you guys! I'm sorry I haven't written in a while. There's a lot of
fun stuff happening in Gobo so look forward to my next email!

I love you!!!!!

--000000000000a8fc13064827ee7d
